# LOCAL run (2026-11-09; user, asked whether to give the critic DrQ's input projection:
# "Yes, then test locally"): slurm/local_c0ft_t05_sac_plain_rw.env (the plain-SAC c0
# fine-tune with uniform-random start steps) with every critic reading
# [h | state] through DrQ's head -- Linear -> 50 -> LayerNorm -> tanh -- and the action
# concatenated after it (CRITIC_PROJ_DIM=50). Encoder, observation and c0's actor are
# unchanged; c0's critics were never trained, so the critics start fresh either way.
# Why: in every trained critic measured -- the c0 fine-tune at 25k/50k/150k and run Q at
# 25k/500k (from scratch, random actions) -- the 2 actions were weighted like 2 of the
# 3652 inputs and drove < 0.4% of the first layer's input variance even for
# uniform-random actions, so Q was ~V(s) and SAC's actor (which learns only from dQ/da)
# chased noise. With the head the action is 2 of 52 first-layer inputs.
. "$REPO/slurm/local_c0ft_t05_sac_plain_rw.env"
export CRITIC_PROJ_DIM=50
